Small fixtures for FreeWRL behaviour that was broken or is platform-sensitive.
Each file says what a pass looks like in its header comment or <meta description>.
They render in any X3D browser, so tools/visual-test/compare.sh can score them against
X_ITE, e.g.  tools/visual-test/compare.sh regression/route_dotted.wrl

route_dotted.wrl       classic VRML "ROUTE a.b TO c.d" (6.7 parser regression, all platforms)
route_malformed.wrl    bad ROUTE statements are reported, not a crash (same parser path)
hanim_skin.x3d         HAnim skinning, static joint rotation (CPU skinning on macOS)
hanim_anim.x3d         HAnim skinning driven by an interpolator
lineproperties.x3d     LineProperties widths and a dashed line type
cubemap_generated.x3d  GeneratedCubeMapTexture (framebuffer + cube map render)
shadows_*.x3d          light shadows TRUE: directional and spot (2D depth map), point (cube depth map)
texture_formats.wrl    JPEG, PNG and GIF ImageTexture
x3d_meta.x3d           X3D <meta> tags in <head> (6.7 parser crash, all platforms)
glcore_stale_attribs.wrl  vertex attribute arrays left enabled across draws (macOS 4.1 core; crashed on CI's software renderer)
